te Unpivoting, and Jurisdictional Topology Schem{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"62b652b4-3c1d-4872-b503-ea47cea1aa0d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"# /wayfinder-read-and-plan: Functional Specification Ingestion, Architectural Decision Mapping, and Edit Planning Governance\n\n**Run ID:** `20261012T231057-024-zqga`  \n**Governing Specification:** [`functional_specification_003.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/functional_specification_003.md)  \n**System Taxonomy Reference:** [`LANGUAGE.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/LANGUAGE.md)  \n**Planning Node Role:** `planning node (feature-planning meta-prompt)`  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Functionality Understanding Check (`/functionality-understanding-check`)\n\n### 1.1. Core System Objective (`{functionality}`)\nThe desired `{functionality}` is the construction of a deterministic, continuously hydratable **Multi-Tier Policy Knowledge Graph Data Pipeline**. Taking a single string query parameter (`{Policy Keyword}`, e.g., `\"LTA\"`), the pipeline programmatically navigates five dependent tiers across authoritative federal legislative, statutory, administrative, and clinical datasets:\n\n1. **Tier 1: Legislative Origins:** Queries Congress.gov API v3 (`/bill`) across historical sessions to isolate advocacy bills (e.g., H.R. 3630, S. 1315) and enacted omnibus vehicles (e.g., Public Law 117-328 via H.R. 2617).\n2. **Tier 2: Statutory Codification Delta:** Ingests GPO GovInfo USLM XML packages to isolate amendatory sections via structural XPath (`//division[@id='FF']/title[@id='IV']/section[@id='4133']`), extracting codified additions to Title 42 of the United States Code (`USC-42-1395x-s-2-JJ`).\n3. **Tier 3: Administrative Directives:** Queries Federal Register API v1 for Final Rules (`2023-24455`, `88 FR 77676`) citing statutory authority, isolating CMS Change Request directives (`CMS-CR-13286`), operational classifications (`CATG == \"LC\"`), cited PubMed literature (`PMID 31454178`), and the governing Medicare Coverage Database Policy Article reference (`A59508`).\n4. **Tier 4A: Clinical Coverage \u0026 Diagnostic Constraints:** Ingests CMS Medicare Coverage Database (MCD) Policy Article `A59508` (*Joint DME MAC Policy Article*), establishing the explicit legal bridge:\n   - `(ChangeRequest)-[:MANDATES_POLICY]-\u003e(CoveragePolicy)`\n   - `(CoveragePolicy)-[:GOVERNS]-\u003e(HCPCSCode)`\n   - `(CoveragePolicy)-[:ALLOWS_DIAGNOSIS]-\u003e(ICD10Code)`\n   - **Prohibition:** Strictly prohibits direct edges between [`HCPCSCode`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-004.md) and [`ICD10Code`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-004.md).\n5. **Tier 4B: Geographic Fee Schedule Normalization:** Filters CMS DMEPOS fee schedule matrix (`phase4_cms_dmepos_lc_category.csv`) to rows matching `CATG == \"LC\"`. Models the 4 standard DME MAC Jurisdictions (`JURIS-DME-A`, `B`, `C`, `D`) and unpivots all 108 state pricing columns (54 jurisdictions: 50 states + DC + PR + VI; Rural `[R]` and Non-Rural `[NR]`) into discrete [`FeeScheduleEntry`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-005.md) records where `fee_amount \u003e 0.00`.\n6. **Tier 5: Contextual Enrichment:** Dispatches parallel queries across the Senate LDA API (lobbying filings), CBO Cost Estimates API (10-year scorekeeping), and NCBI PubMed E-Utilities API (peer-reviewed clinical studies).\n\n### 1.2. Architecture Refinement: Distinguishing Continuous Hydration from Benchmark Oracles\nAddressing the gap identified in [`basic_corrections.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/basic_corrections.md), the system is designed not as a static script hardcoded to 22 benchmark files, but as a generalized, multi-tenant property graph engine:\n- **Root Anchor:** Every run instantiates or updates a root [`Policy`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-001.md) vertex (`POLICY-[keyword]`) anchoring search keyword, execution run ID, and timestamp.\n- **Idempotent Upserts (`MERGE` Semantics):** When new policies are ingested, overlapping federal nodes (e.g., Public Law 117-328, DME MAC Jurisdictions) are deduplicated and updated in place via deterministic primary keys without duplicating vertices or edges.\n- **Universal Edge Provenance:** 100% of edges in the graph carry four mandatory attributes: `source_uri`, `selector`, `ingestion_timestamp`, and `run_id`.\n- **System Invariants:** Fully enforced under `INV-FAIL-FAST`, `INV-NO-KEYWORD-BRIDGING`, `INV-UNBROKEN-ANCESTRY`, `INV-50-STATE-COMPLETENESS`, and `INV-IDEMPOTENT-UPSERTS`.\n- **Benchmark Role:** The empirical files in `DataSources_Agent/assets/20261012T213134-452-7663/` serve as the acceptance oracle.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Wayfinder Map \u0026 Architecture Initialization\n\nThe canonical roadmap has been initialized and saved to [`wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/map.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/map.md).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    T001[\"ticket-001.md: Phase 1 Legislative Genesis \u0026 Policy Root\\n(Congress.gov API v3 -\u003e Policy, Bill, PublicLaw)\"]\n    T002[\"ticket-002.md: Phase 2 Statutory Codification\\n(GPO GovInfo USLM XML -\u003e StatutorySection)\"]\n    T003[\"ticket-003.md: Phase 3 Administrative Directives\\n(Federal Register API v1 \u0026 CMS Portal -\u003e Regulation, ChangeRequest)\"]\n    T004[\"ticket-004.md: Phase 4A Coverage Policy \u0026 Diagnostic Constraints\\n(CMS MCD Policy Article A59508 -\u003e CoveragePolicy, HCPCSCode, ICD10Code)\"]\n    T005[\"ticket-005.md: Phase 4B Geographic Fee Schedule Normalization\\n(CMS DMEPOS CSV -\u003e 4 Jurisdictions, 54 States, FeeScheduleEntry Records)\"]\n    T006[\"ticket-006.md: Phase 5 Contextual Enrichment\\n(Senate LDA API, CBO API, NCBI PubMed API -\u003e Filings, Scores, Studies)\"]\n    T007[\"ticket-007.md: End-to-End Graph Assembly \u0026 Provenance\\n(Graph Topology, Provenance Engine, Invariant Verification)\"]\n\n    T001 --\u003e|Enacted_Law_ID| T002\n    T001 --\u003e|Target_Bill_IDs| T006\n    T002 --\u003e|US_Code_Citations| T003\n    T003 --\u003e|Coverage_Policy_ID| T004\n    T003 --\u003e|Operational_Filters| T005\n    T003 --\u003e|Clinical_Citations| T006\n    T004 --\u003e|HCPCSCode Nodes| T005\n    T001 \u0026 T002 \u0026 T003 \u0026 T004 \u0026 T005 \u0026 T006 --\u003e T007\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Atomic Decision Tickets (`wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/`)\n\nAll seven decision tickets have been authored with monotonically increasing counters inside the run directory, resolving candidate datasources, endpoint operational parameters, target schemas, field access classifications, and node/edge contracts:\n\n1. [`ticket-001.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-001.md): **Phase 1 Legislative Genesis, Bill Resolution, and Root Policy Ingestion Schema**\n   - Locks Congress.gov API v3 (`/bill`, `/actions`, `/relatedbills`).\n   - Defines [`Policy`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-001.md), [`Bill`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261012T231057-024-zqga/wayfinder/20261012T231057-024-zqga/tickets/ticket-001.md), [`PublicLaw`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-pla